SUMMARY:(Overnight) Fall Foliage XXI: Cataloochee- GSMNP
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nJoin THOG for its 21st ann
 ual Fall Foliage Event which will include a hike to Hemphill Bald and Elk 
 Watching. We will be car camping at a group site in the Cataloochee area t
 his year at Great Smoky Mountains National Park. No oversized tents\, plea
 se. We’ll hike to Hemphill Bald\, an approximately 10 mile out and back 
 hike with an elevation gain of around 1\,800 FT. We’ll be rewarded with 
 a beautiful 180 degree view of the Smokies at the summit. We will have lun
 ch at the summit as well.\n**Before you RSVP\, please make sure you read t
 his event description completely!**\n\nWhen you RSVP\, you will be asked a
  Three-Part Question that needs to be answered. THOG Organizers\, feel fre
 e to sign yourself up for this event at anytime. More spots will be opened
  on September 1st.\nHiking shoes or boots are highly recommended due to th
 e terrain. Be sure to bring your own camping gear\, i.e.\, tent\, pad\, sl
 eeping bag\, etc.\n\nThe highlights of this trip include the Fall Colors\,
  views from Hemphill Bald and Elk watching.\n**Carpooling is necessary and
  carpools will meet on Friday at 9AM in Chapel Hill. This remote campsite 
 can only hold 5 cars. Camping is for 2 nights.** **Only vehicles that will
  have at least 3-4 attendees will be allowed to park at the campsite.** We
 ’ll discuss carpool options as the trip gets closer.\n\nYOUR RSVP IS YOU
 R COMMITMENT TO THIS TRIP. Late cancellations (cancellations made within 7
  days of the event) or no shows without an emergency will be noted in your
  THOG account and could affect future rsvp's. Prior late cancellations and
  no-shows may affect your RSVP to this event.\n\nBe sure to bring enough f
 ood for meals/snacks for Friday dinner through at least breakfast Sunday. 
 The temperatures in this area are typically chilly by this time so bring c
 lothing layers- jacket\, gloves\, and hat. There are bathrooms but no show
 ers.\nApproximate costs per person for camping and firewood will be $5-$10
  based on about 18 participants.\n\nThis is bear territory. Food and items
  with scents (i.e toothpaste\, lotions\, etc.) must be properly stored.\n*
 *Full details will be sent to participants via email or Meetup message aft
 er RSVP's close.** Failure to respond to the email will result in your RSV
 P being removed.\nIf you are on the Waitlist\, make sure you check your st
 atus in case you are added to the "Going" list.\n\nBy participating in thi
 s event\, you agree to the terms below:\nTRIP PARTICIPANT WAIVER OF LIABIL
 ITY I fully realize that this activity involves a risk of personal injury\
 , property damage\, or loss of my person or property. I hereby for myself\
 , my heirs\, executors and administrators\, and same for persons with whom
  are in my party\, waive and release any claims or rights against Triangle
  Hiking & Outdoors Group (THOG)\, all of its owners and coordinators for a
 ny and all injury\, damages or loss to my person or property incurred duri
 ng this activity. I also understand that THOG organizers are not required\
 , nor should it be assumed that they are CPR/First Aid/Wilderness Survival
  Certified and I am responsible for my own personal safety.\nQuestions abo
 ut this event?\nPlease comment below or send me a Meetup message.\n-Triang
 le Hiking and Outdoors Group & Larredo
